  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to deeming the objects or purposes for which certain bonds were issued by the city of Buffalo to be for the construction of an archway and infrastructure improvements at the intersection of Michigan avenue and Broadway within said city and authorizing the expenditure of the proceeds from such bonds for such objects or purposes",
    "basePrintNo": "S4427",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4427-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Bonds and Notes",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4427\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act in relation to deeming the objects or purposes for which\ncertain bonds were issued by the city of Buffalo to be for the\nconstruction of an archway and infrastructure improvements at the\nintersection of Michigan avenue and Broadway within said city and\nauthorizing the expenditure of the proceeds from such bonds for such\nobjects or purposes\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nAuthorizes bond proceeds to be used for construction and\ninfrastructure improvements at the intersection of Michigan Avenue and\nBroadway in the City of Buffalo\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one puts forth Legislative Findings that the City of Buffalo\nissued a bond on April 17, 2012 and that the resolution failed to\ninclude language regarding the construction of an archway at the\nintersection of the City where the archway construction were intended\nto be made.\n\nSection two authorizes a new purpose for such bonds.\n\nSection three provides for permissive referendum on the new purpose of\nthe bonds.\n\nSection four provides for a separability clause. Section five provides\nan immediate effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nDue to an administrative error that occurred during the preparation of\nassociated documents, the Common Council of the City of Buffalo\nadopted on February 23, 2012 a bond resolution authorizing the\nissuance of City bonds in the amount of $150,000 to finance the cost\nof constructing the Archway Project at non-existent location, that\nbeing the intersection of Michigan Avenue and Jefferson Avenue.\n\nIn order to correct this error, legislation must be enacted to\nauthorize the Common Council to amend the Bond Resolution and\nauthorize financing for construction of the Archway Project at the\nintended Michigan Avenue and Broadway Street location.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew legislation.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
